      "id": "claim_7f2dfd61cb3e4d3eb4577088e2e0533e",
      "statement": "The CLI's investigation-creation path is split across two commands that both call the create-investigation Lambda with a SigV4-signed AWS SDK client: `investigation create` (internal/cmd/create_investigation.go) invokes it with skip_task=true to provision or reuse only the EFS access point, while `session create` (internal/cmd/start_session.go) invokes it without that flag to also launch the ECS Fargate task, deriving the session/task ID from the returned task ARN and the SRE role ARN from the response (falling back to the profile's configured role only if the Lambda omits one). The Lambda itself (lambda/create-investigation/handler.py) validates the OIDC operator and required group membership before dispatching to a shared routine that provisions or reuses an investigation EFS access point and can launch a Fargate task using a per-investigation task definition derived from the regional task definition.",
