      "id": "claim_d5a3037869d34ec8a3503ee03f222c01",
      "statement": "Trusted Actions' own HCP Terraform workspaces and Tekton build pipelines were imported as files only, but the committed configuration already reflects a rebind to this repository rather than the original one: hcp-terraform/rosa-trusted-actions/main.tf's rosa-trusted-actions-global and rosa-trusted-actions-stage workspaces both declare github_repo_name = \"rosa-boundary\" and working directories under components/trusted-actions/terraform/{global,regional}, and the copied .tekton/rosa-trusted-actions-push.yaml and rosa-trusted-actions-pull-request.yaml pipelines no longer carry a `false &&` guard on their on-cel-expression trigger -- both evaluate normally for push/PR events touching components/trusted-actions/*** or the pipeline file, though a retained comment (\"Enable only at the coordinated cutover after checking the shared image/release destination\") records the earlier pre-cutover state rather than an active guard. Both pipelines still publish to quay.io/redhat-user-workloads/rosa-tenant/rosa-trusted-actions (push and on-pr tags). None of this proves Trusted Actions' current live HCP run state, Prow/Tide merge behavior, or Konflux build/release bindings have moved -- only the committed Terraform/Tekton configuration is described; live platform state must be verified separately.",
